                {
                  "dsDescriptionValue": {
                    "typeName": "dsDescriptionValue",
                    "multiple": false,
                    "typeClass": "primitive",
                    "value": "PWT version 11.0 is a database with information on relative levels of income, output, input and productivity, covering 185 countries between 1950 and 2023. For questions not covered in the documentation, please contact <a href=\"mailto:pwt@rug.nl\">pwt@rug.nl</a>.<br><br>\n\n<b>When using these data (for whatever purpose), please make the following reference:</b><br>\nFeenstra, Robert C., Robert Inklaar and Marcel P. Timmer (2015), \"The Next Generation of the Penn World Table\" American Economic Review, 105(10), 3150-3182, <a href=\"https://www.doi.org/10.1257/aer.20130954\" target=\"_blank\">DOI: 10.1257/aer.20130954</a>, available for download at <a href=\"http://www.ggdc.net/pwt\" target=\"_blank\">www.ggdc.net/pwt</a><br><br>\n\nMore information about this release of the Penn World Table can be found on the <a href=\"https://www.rug.nl/ggdc/productivity/pwt/pwt-releases/pwt110\" target=\"_blank\">associated page</a> on the website of the <a href=\"https://www.rug.nl/ggdc/\" target=\"_blank\">Groningen Growth and Development Centre</a>.<br><br>\nThis research has been supported by the <a href=\"https://steg.cepr.org/\" target=\"_blank\">STEG project</a>, a research initiative funded by the UK Government’s Foreign, Commonwealth and Development Office."
                  },
                  "dsDescriptionDate": {
